# Getting started

1. Install [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/), then in the repo: `uv sync`.
{%- if privacy_hook %}
2. Turn on the pre-commit hook: `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`.
{%- endif %}
3. Copy `{{ 'config.example.toml' if config_style == 'toml' else '.env.example' }}` to `{{ 'config.toml' if config_style == 'toml' else '.env' }}` and fill it in. It is gitignored.
4. Load data: `uv run {{ project_name }} ingest <files>`, then `uv run {{ project_name }} status`.
5. Open the app: `uv run {{ project_name }} app`, then http://localhost:{{ app_port }}.
{%- if tailnet %}

## On your other devices (Tailscale)

`uv run {{ project_name }} app --tailnet` also serves the app at `https://<this machine's tailnet name>:{{ app_port }}`,
for as long as it runs. Only devices on your tailnet can open it.
{%- endif %}
{%- if motherduck %}

## MotherDuck

Make a token in MotherDuck (Settings → Access tokens) and put it in {{ '`[motherduck] token` in config.toml' if config_style == 'toml' else '`MOTHERDUCK_TOKEN` in .env' }}. Then
`/publish` (or `uv run {{ project_name }} publish`) copies the contract views to `md:{{ motherduck_db }}`.
{%- endif %}
{%- if cloud_run %}

## Cloud Run

docs/hosting.md: the one-time setup, then `/hosting deploy`.
{%- endif %}

## Claude Code

The skills in `.claude/skills/` run the common tasks: `/app`{% if motherduck %}, `/publish`{% endif %}{% if backup %}, `/backup`{% endif %}{% if cloud_run %}, `/hosting`{% endif %}, `/catch-up`,
`/scaffold-update`.
